  biomeName: The Ash-Wastes
  minDepthMeters: 8750
  maxDepthMeters: 9275
  shortDescription: Deep ash deposits that storm when disturbed.
  isPlaceholder: 0
  visitPurpose: Deep-pressure biome. Come here with purpose, stronger gear, and a
    plan to follow strong natural shapes and search obvious pockets.
  commonRewardHook: Even routine value here comes from Abyssal Crystal and Thermal
    Gel.
  rareRewardHook: 'The reason to risk the trip is: Tungsten Chunk and Abyss Pressure
    Shell.'
  landmarkIdentity: The Ash-Wastes reads through spires, steps, and big natural crowns.
    Landmarks should feel scarce but memorable.
  safePocketIdentity: 'Safe pockets are short-lived and mostly procedural: a lee
    side, a bowl edge, a dead current seam.'
  riskSummary: 'Main failure mode: bad drops and exposed lines, depth stress, and
    expensive hesitation. Creature pressure stays extreme.'
  extractionFocus: 'High-risk extraction under thermal and survival pressure. Deep
    tier: favor stone pockets and hard-form nodes, extract only what justifies the
    risk, and leave cleanly.'
  landmarkGuidance: Dominant landmark is magma seam or hadal chimney crown. This
    slot should read through red-black catastrophic skyline; use vertical forms to
    keep heading.
